                "id": 180850836,
                "type": "DiffNote",
                "body": "⚠️ **卸载步骤指示写入 {\"permissions\":{\"allow\":[]}} 会覆盖 settings.json 的其他字段**\n\n第 125 行指示：当 `permissions.allow` 数组被清空后，写入 `{\"permissions\":{\"allow\":[]}}`。但 `.claude/settings.json` 是 Claude Code 的综合配置文件，除 `permissions` 外可能还包含 `hooks`、`env`、`model`、`statusLine` 等顶层字段。按字面理解 `write {\"permissions\":{\"allow\":[]}}` 即把整个文件内容覆写为该 JSON，其他字段（如用户配置的 hooks、env 变量）将全部丢失。这与同一句中的安全护栏 `never delete the file or null out the structure` 自相矛盾——覆写为仅含 permissions 的对象本质上就是破坏了原有结构。该矛盾源于指令未区分「仅更新 permissions 字段」与「覆写整个文件」两种语义，导致严格按字面执行的代理可能在清空 allow 数组时意外删除用户的其他配置。\n\n**上下文代码**:\n```\nTo do the surgical edit, read `.claude/settings.json`, filter the `permissions.allow` array to drop only the matched entries (string equality, including the resolved `<PLUGIN_DIR>`), and write it back. If the array becomes empty, write `{\"permissions\":{\"allow\":[]}}` — never delete the file or null out the structure.\n```\n\n**修复方案**:\n```\nTo do the surgical edit, read `.claude/settings.json`, parse it as JSON, filter the `permissions.allow` array to drop only the matched entries (string equality, including the resolved `<PLUGIN_DIR>`), and write the full object back preserving every other top-level field (hooks, env, model, etc.). If the `allow` array becomes empty, set `permissions.allow` to `[]` while still preserving all non-`permissions` fields — never delete the file, never overwrite non-`permissions` fields, and never null out the structure.\n```\n明确区分「更新 permissions 字段」与「覆写整个文件」两种语义：始终以解析-修改-写回的方式操作 settings.json，仅修改 `permissions.allow` 数组，其他顶层字段原样保留。把原指令中容易引起整文件覆写的 `write {\"permissions\":{\"allow\":[]}}` 改为 `set permissions.allow to []`，并显式列出需保留的字段类别（hooks/env/model 等），消除语义歧义，避免代理在边界情况下意外删除用户的其他配置。\n\n**官方参考资料**:\n- [Python os.path documentation](https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.path.html)\n- [Python File I/O best practices](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/inputoutput.html#reading-and-writing-files)\n\n\n\n---\n🤖 generated by ai@claude",
